src/providers/mongodb.provider.js
Responsibility

This file has one job only:

Talk to MongoDB Atlas Data API.

It knows:

MongoDB URL
API Key
Database Name
Collection Name

It does not know:

Users
OTP
Email
Authentication
Public API

Every repository will call only these methods:

findOne()

insertOne()

updateOne()

deleteOne()

findMany()

Repositories never call fetch() directly.

They always go through the provider.
Example Architecture
register.service.js
        │
        ▼
user.repository.js
        │
        ▼
mongodb.provider.js
        │
        ▼
MongoDB Atlas Data API
Why is this better?

Suppose after one year you move from:

MongoDB Atlas

to

Supabase

or

Firebase

Only this file changes.

Everything else stays exactly the same.

That's why companies use this pattern.



One more thing (important)

I also want to improve our project.

Instead of just building a backend, we'll make it publishable as an NPM package later.

Imagine being able to do this in any future project:

npm install @rishabh/auth

and instantly have:

Email OTP
JWT Authentication
Login
Registration
Password Reset
Middleware

That means while we're building this backend, we're also designing it to be reusable across your future SaaS, portfolio, e-commerce, NFT, and CRM projects.

I think that's a much more valuable end goal than building something that's tied to a single application.


